{"content":[{"c":["JAIR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Descendant of Manasseh (",{"href":"?bref=Num.32.41","r":"Num.32.41","rawR":"Num.32.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.32.41","value":"Num.32.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 32:41"},"), who at the time of the Conquest took several villages in the Argob region of Bashan and Gilead and called them after his own name, Havvoth-jair, meaning “Towns of Jair” (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.3.14","r":"Deut.3.14","rawR":"Deut.3.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.3.14","value":"Deut.3.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 3:14"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.30","r":"Josh.13.30","rawR":"Josh.13.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.30","value":"Josh.13.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 13:30"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.13","r":"1Kgs.4.13","rawR":"1Kgs.4.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.13","value":"1Kgs.4.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 4:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.23","r":"1Chr.2.23","rawR":"1Chr.2.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.23","value":"1Chr.2.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:23"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=HavothJairHavvothJair_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"HavothJairHavvothJair_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"HavothJairHavvothJair_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Havoth-jair, Havvoth-jair"},"."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["2. One of the judges of Israel. He judged Israel 22 years. His being a Gileadite makes it probable that he was a descendant of #1 above (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.10.3-5","r":"Judg.10.3-5","rawR":"Judg.10.3-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.10.3-5","value":"Judg.10.3-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 10:3-5"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Father of Elhanan, who killed Lahmi, Goliath’s brother (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.20.5","r":"1Chr.20.5","rawR":"1Chr.20.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.20.5","value":"1Chr.20.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 20:5"},"). In ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.21.19","r":"2Sam.21.19","rawR":"2Sam.21.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.21.19","value":"2Sam.21.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Samuel 21:19"}," he is called Jaare-oregim."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Father of Mordecai (",{"href":"?bref=Esth.2.5","r":"Esth.2.5","rawR":"Esth.2.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Esth.2.5","value":"Esth.2.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Est 2:5"},"). Because of the time lapse from the capture of Jeconiah, king of Judah (597 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"), to the beginning of the reign of Xerxes, king of Persia (486 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"), Jair was either the one taken captive with Jeconiah or his father, Shimei, was, in which case Jair would have been born during the Captivity."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Jair","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 32:41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.32.41","rawQueryValue":"Num.32.41","sourceRefExact":"Num.32.41"},{"anchorText":"Dt 3:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.3.14","rawQueryValue":"Deut.3.14","sourceRefExact":"Deut.3.14"},{"anchorText":"Jos 13:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.30","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.30","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.30"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 4:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.13","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.13","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.13"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.23","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.23","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.23"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 10:3-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.10.3-5","rawQueryValue":"Judg.10.3-5","sourceRefExact":"Judg.10.3-5"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 20:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.20.5","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.20.5","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.20.5"},{"anchorText":"2 Samuel 21:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.21.19","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.21.19","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.21.19"},{"anchorText":"Est 2:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Esth.2.5","rawQueryValue":"Esth.2.5","sourceRefExact":"Esth.2.5"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"00e9883bbac2c629c0c7ee181911758f3c006822e0abf626032df391cafbd787","sourceItemName":"Jair","sourceItemOrder":59,"sourceMember":"Articles/J.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Jair","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Jair","title":"Jair","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}